  "problem": "There are two groups of people In a small town: those who travel to work by car and those who travel by train. Every year a study is done in which people are asked about their preference between using trains versus cars. The table below shows the results of this study.\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Car** | **Train** |\n| To: | **Car** | $0.35$ | $0.25$ |\n| **Train** | $0.65$ | $0.75$ |  |\n\nIt's found that $65%$ of people who currently travel by car will switch to train next year, while $25%$ of people who currently travel by train will switch to their car next year.\n\nAssuming that the town has $90\\,000$ people that travel to work by train or car, and the given probabilities remain constant over many years, how many people will eventually use the train to travel to work?",
